{
"dur": 58.715,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.918,
"text": "That same day, Germany attacked the Netherlands, Belgium, Luxembourg and France, with around three million soldiers and thousands of tanks and planes.",
"end": 8.193
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.193,
"vo_start": 8.468,
"vo_end": 15.905,
"text": "Group B swept into the Netherlands and Belgium, drawing the best British and French troops north. Group C sat facing the Maginot Line.",
"end": 16.18
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 16.18,
"vo_start": 16.455,
"vo_end": 24.415,
"text": "Group A was the real plan. Its tanks drove through the Ardennes, a thick, hilly forest French generals thought tanks could never cross.",
"end": 24.69
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 24.69,
"vo_start": 24.965,
"vo_end": 29.965,
"text": "They broke through at Sedan on 13 May and raced to the sea. The Allied armies in the north were cut off.",
"end": 30.24
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 30.24,
"vo_start": 30.515,
"vo_end": 34.475,
"text": "Hundreds of thousands of soldiers were trapped on the beaches at Dunkirk with the sea at their backs.",
"end": 34.75
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 34.75,
"vo_start": 35.025,
"vo_end": 43.425,
"text": "From 26 May, Britain sent everything that could float: navy ships, ferries, fishing boats, pleasure yachts. Fighter planes covered them overhead.",
"end": 43.7
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 43.7,
"vo_start": 43.975,
"vo_end": 50.175,
"text": "By 4 June about 338,000 soldiers had been rescued. But they left almost all their tanks and guns behind.",
"end": 50.45
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 50.45,
"vo_start": 50.725,
"vo_end": 57.765,
"text": "Italy's dictator, Mussolini, joined Hitler and declared war on 10 June. On 22 June 1940 France signed an armistice.",
"end": 58.715
}
],
